	'k0335d84f' => '30% of first-year base + target bonus',
	'k034dda50' => 'We established Senbatsu Partners in 2012 around one central principle: executive search requires uncompromised personal accountability. Because our partners limit their individual workloads to 6 simultaneous searches, they never delegate critical interviews or candidate referencing to junior associates. Two partners attend every half-day brief session to challenge assumptions and clarify the brief. Every candidate presented on our shortlist of 3 has been interviewed in depth by the partner leading the search. This structure ensures that when clients call our Amsterdam office, they speak directly with the partner who knows the market, understands the corporate governance landscape, and carries full responsibility for the search outcome.',
	'k03de7667' => 'The six-search rule and partner continuity',
	'k067c7f34' => 'Confidentiality is the bedrock of retained executive search. We recognize that senior leadership transitions frequently involve sensitive corporate governance, succession planning, or strategic market repositioning. Client names are never published on our website, in promotional materials, or in Search notes letters. During the initial outreach phase of weeks 1 to 4, candidate discussions are conducted under mutual non-disclosure, with your corporate identity revealed only after a candidate has been vetted by the lead partner and signed an explicit non-disclosure agreement. Search dossiers are numbered, stored securely, and destroyed upon assignment completion, protecting total discretion throughout.',
