	'k0e5e1efd' => 'Two partners spend a half day at your office to establish role requirements, reporting lines, and the line we will not cross, producing a written brief before anyone is approached.',
	'k10b96a5f' => 'Tomás leads operations and plant searches and spends time on the shop floor before he writes a brief. He is present at every offer conversation he runs.',
	'k11f3fbd4' => 'From our single office in Amsterdam, we conduct searches across the Benelux, Germany, France, the Nordics and Iberia, as well as European remote leadership appointments. Our focus centres on four core environments: People, Europe, Boards and Industry. Whether advising industrial manufacturers, medical device enterprises, software firms or family-owned logistics groups, we remain deliberately compact. We do not maintain satellite branches or cross-selling networks. Compensation is completely transparent: clients pay a retainer in three milestone instalments, with no hidden margins or placement bonuses. We believe that executive search functions best as a quiet, disciplined craft practiced by experienced partners who understand the long-term governance consequences of every leadership appointment.',
	'k1228cccc' => 'Industrial',
	'k12520113' => 'Senbatsu Partners operates from a single office located at Oostelijke Handelskade 1210, 1019 BL Amsterdam, Netherlands. Our team is available by email at search@senbatsu-partners.example and telephone at +31 20 555 0142. Our office hours are Monday through Friday, 08:30 to 18:00 CET. Client office manager Claire Duval coordinates all appointments, contract documentation, and partner diaries. Because our partners maintain strict delivery standards, formal half-day brief sessions are held on Tuesdays and Thursdays. When you contact our office regarding a senior vacancy, a search partner will review your initial details and reply directly within two working days.',
	'k13467992' => 'Published once every quarter, Search notes delivers concise, candid observations on senior executive recruitment, board governance, and leadership succession across Europe. Rather than summarizing industry news, each letter examines actual dilemmas encountered during our retained searches: balancing founder authority with independent non-executive oversight, restructuring executive compensation in volatile markets, or maintaining client boundaries during sensitive market mapping. We share practical lessons drawn directly from our Amsterdam search practice, anonymised to protect client privacy. It is written specifically for chairs, chief executives, and founders who evaluate senior leadership talent.',
