	'k31be07e7' => 'Retained search fees are invoiced in three equal instalments: one third upon contract signing, one third upon delivery of the shortlist of 3 candidates by week 6, and the final third upon candidate acceptance and signed offer. All fee amounts are expressed in EUR and exclude statutory VAT. If a client cancels an ongoing mandate, instalments already paid are non-refundable, recognizing the substantial market mapping and candidate referencing completed to that stage. However, the initial €4,800 brief session fee is credited in full against the search fee once the search commences. Expenses for client-requested travel and formal psychometric assessment tools are billed strictly at cost, subject to our 8% cap.',
	'k342dacf2' => 'Iberia',
	'k34442a57' => 'Every search begins with a mandatory half-day brief session conducted on site at the client office. Two partners attend this working meeting to evaluate corporate governance, organizational dynamics, reporting lines, and the specific mandate expectations. We explore both what the leadership role requires and what the organisation must avoid. The output is a rigorous written role brief that defines candidate competencies and explicitly establishes the line we will not cross regarding off-limits companies and non-negotiable requirements. No prospective candidates are approached until this brief document is formally reviewed, agreed upon, and signed off by both client and partner.',
	'k3617caf1' => 'We define our search assignments through three clear dimensions: function, sector, and region. Functionally, we operate in Finance, Operations, Legal, Technology, People, and General Management. Our sector experience is anchored in Logistics, Medical Devices, Industrial Manufacturing, Software, Food Production, and Family-Owned Groups. Regionally, we accept mandates headquartered or operating within the Benelux, Germany, France, the Nordics, and Iberia, as well as European remote leadership structures. By confining our scope to these specific functions and geographies, Jonas Weber and our research team maintain live intelligence on candidate performance across regional competitors. We do not accept assignments outside these sectors where we cannot construct an exhaustive, high-conviction market map.',
