	'k5014afd8' => 'Integrity in executive search requires knowing when to refuse work. We decline volume hiring projects, contingent search arrangements, and roles below director level. We never accept a search without conducting an in-person brief session and securing a signed role brief that establishes clear hiring criteria. Crucially, we reject mandates that demand approaching individuals employed by our existing clients, and we refuse any situation where two firms are hired to compete on the same seat. Restricting our practice in this manner protects our clients from compromised candidate pools and prevents conflicts of interest. When we accept a search, our partners dedicate uninterrupted effort to filling that single seat.',
