	'k9eafb53d' => 'How a search runs',
	'ka05d65e1' => 'Helena Marsh founded Senbatsu Partners in Amsterdam in 2012 to provide boards and chief executives with an undivided advisory relationship. When you commission a search, the partner who leads the initial brief session conducts the market mapping, interviews prospective candidates, and remains present at the offer table. To maintain rigor and focus, each partner manages at most six searches at any given time.',
